title DAHL-J12r2 data_dignity_signed — the two succession proofs bound to settled identities
prompt Continue the loop: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think r1 fixed succession as a pure two-proof state machine. r2's crux (from the Journey 12 exploration): bind each proof to a settled Kumara identity so a steward cannot seal in a departed keeper's name or record an acceptance the heir never gave. Mirrored council_sky_signed / skate_group_signed.
think Two distinct signed acts: the keeper's directive signs tag+estate_id+keeper+heir+will_digest (a SHA-256 over every willed item and its disposition, in order); the heir's acceptance signs tag+estate_id+keeper+heir. Distinct tags so a seal is never replayed as an acceptance; estate_id so neither crosses estates.
think The honesty crux is the will digest: seal_signed recomputes the digest from the estate's current marks and checks the keeper's signature over it, so a bequeathed→rested tamper after signing falls BadConsent — a steward cannot rewrite a departed keeper's will. Added two pub readers to r1 (item_at, disposition_at) so r2 can digest the marks — additive, r1 re-runs GREEN.
